  "notes": "Agent re-read after the Code Health refactor, 2026-11-07, under the owner directive transcribed in verification/reviews/rulings/agent-rereview-after-refactor-2026-11-07.md. This record is NOT an owner signature: it attests the agent's substantive reading only. Read http_profile.fleet_strict_store_class, proxy.replay_admission_gate and proxy.replay_tier_production_minimum. The production sources of the first two (mcp-re-http-profile/src/dispatch.rs and dispatch/replay_posture.rs; mcp-re-proxy/src/http_profile_dispatch.rs and http_profile_dispatch/core_projection.rs) have no diff since the last review, and neither do their in-source tests. In replay_tier.rs only the tests changed: the parse-refusal, wire-name and strict-minimum assertions became table loops over the same cases with the same expected values (wait-quorum and linearizable meet the minimum; the async and single-store tiers do not). The cited integration tests in http_profile_dispatch_test.rs are identical body for body; the two cited dispatch_test tests differ only in building their verified evidence through verified_from_client_a, which passes the same key, key id, fresh nonce and block. The claim, scope and premises (ASM-0040, ASM-0041 as registered) are unchanged. Evidence class as registered; V0 units are tested and probed, not machine-checked proofs. The mutation lane was not re-run by this reading; check-registries resolves every probe anchor.",
